@@ -373,3 +373,18 @@ ctest --test-dir build/register-context --output-on-failure
 ```
 
 On Linux x86-64, omit `CMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES`; the full `BUILD_TESTING` build also registers these tests. Apple silicon runs the x86-64 tests through Rosetta. They cover the unwinder's register transfer, not the complete macOS runtime or guest exception handling.
+
+### Linux host-write regression
+
+With `BUILD_TESTING=ON`, build `guest_host_write_hooks_tests`,
+`guest_file_vector_tests`, `guest_file_vector_memory_tests`, `guest_aio_tests`,
+and `guest_aio_registry_tests`. Run:
+
+```sh
+ctest --test-dir build -R '^(guest_host_write_hooks|guest_file_vector|guest_file_vector_memory|guest_aio.*)$' --output-on-failure
+```
+
+The host-write test first verifies that a kernel read into a read-only page
+returns EFAULT, then registers host-write callbacks and verifies scalar,
+positioned, and vectored reads, overlapping-page access, out-of-order scope
+completion, and callback removal while a scope remains active.
